[70.435234, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 release summary\n\nThe calendar clamped every renewal to the 28th and then calculated the next\nrenewal from that shortened date. Proration also assumed 30/365-day periods,\ncredited the old plan at the change-date price, and prorated interval changes\ninstead of starting a full new billing cycle.\n\nChanges:\n- Clamp to the target month's actual last day, including leap years.\n- Calculate cycle boundaries directly from the original anchor, in constant time.\n- Use actual cycle days and the old price in force at cycle start.\n- Keep the anchor for same-interval changes; charge full price and re-anchor on\n  the change date for monthly/annual switches.\n- Round exact integer ratios half-to-even, without Decimal-context precision loss.\n- Add calendar, rounding, and end-to-end CLI regression tests.\n\nValidation: `python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes all 26 tests, including\nbulk repricing within the unchanged 0.2-second budget. All 10 finance worked\nexamples are checke"]
[70.43536, "i", "d through `python -m billing preview`, including negative\ntotals carried as account credit. Public API signatures are unchanged. No known\nfailures were added, and existing fixtures, data, and release controls are unchanged.\nEOF\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[70.435373, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[70.435461, "o", "d through `python -m billing preview`, including negative\r\ntotals carried as account credit. Public API signatures are unchanged. No known\r\nfailures were added, and existing fixtures, data, and release controls are unchanged.\r\nEOF\r\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 release summary"]
